Done. Added `rename` to `src/store.rs:18-54`.

What it does: reads `{old_id}.note`, parses the 4 `SEP`-delimited parts, rewrites the file with `new_id` and `new_title` while reusing the existing pinned flag and body (tags are re-derived from the body, so they're preserved), then deletes the old file.

Edge cases handled:
- `old_id == new_id` → file paths are identical, so the old file isn't deleted (no-op on the file name).
- Missing or malformed old file → returns `Err`.

Verified end-to-end (harness since removed): a note with `#tag1 #tag2`, `pinned=true` renamed to `new1`/`New Title` loads back as exactly one note with the new id/title, unchanged body, tags, and pinned state; `old1.note` is gone; same-id rename keeps the file; renaming a missing note errors. `cargo build` (debug + release) passes.


